# Secrets and local configuration. A committed .env is the most common way a credential
# reaches a public repository: the file is harmless in isolation and the damage is already
# done by the time a scanner notices.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.jks
secrets/

